1
00:00:03,225 --> 00:00:06,295
Back at Search, Indexes, select Add index.

2
00:00:06,295 --> 00:00:10,518
The Available Sources dialog groups the sources by provider.

3
00:00:10,518 --> 00:00:15,571
Under Lucene, Content in Lucene builds an index from the content items of

4
00:00:15,571 --> 00:00:17,555
your site, so select Add.

5
00:00:18,064 --> 00:00:21,912
Index Name is the name of the index in the provider, and it

6
00:00:21,912 --> 00:00:24,398
cannot change once the index exists.

7
00:00:24,398 --> 00:00:29,785
Name is the unique name that the settings, the permission and the search address use.

8
00:00:29,785 --> 00:00:32,804
Type website in Index Name, and Name follows.

9
00:00:33,259 --> 00:00:37,759
Content types lists the types to index, and at least one is required.

10
00:00:37,759 --> 00:00:39,859
Select Blog Post and Article.

11
00:00:39,859 --> 00:00:44,539
Culture stays on Any culture, and the other options keep their defaults.

12
00:00:44,997 --> 00:00:46,004
Select Save.

13
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:51,485
A message confirms that the index was created and that synchronizing runs in the background.

14
00:00:51,485 --> 00:00:55,457
The index appears in the list with the labels Lucene and Content.

